---
layout: null
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
# 18 pages: the pinned /v2/ and the bare latest path, each with one real page
# per result so a shared link can carry its own og: tags. See _data/quizroutes.js
pagination:
  data: quizroutes
  size: 1
  alias: route
permalink: "/which-quantum-interpretation-are-you/{{ route.path }}index.html"
---
{%- set QUIZ = "https://agicook.com/which-quantum-interpretation-are-you/" %}
{%- set SHARE = quiz.meta.share %}
{%- set rev = route.reveal %}
{%- set r = quiz.results[rev] if rev else false %}
{%- set here = QUIZ + route.path %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{% if r %}{{ r.name }} — {{ SHARE.title }}{% else %}{{ SHARE.title }}{% endif %}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{% if r %}{{ r.tagline | replace("“", "") | replace("”", "") }} Ten questions to find out which lump under the carpet is yours.{% else %}Ten questions, six answers and two you have to earn. Every interpretation of quantum mechanics is wild somewhere — this one finds out where you put the weirdness.{% endif %}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ here }}">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="agicook">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ here }}">
<meta property="og:title" content="{% if r %}{{ r.name }} — {{ SHARE.title }}{% else %}{{ SHARE.title }}{% endif %}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{% if r %}{{ r.tagline | replace("“", "") | replace("”", "") }} Find out which lump under the carpet is yours.{% else %}Weirdness is conserved. You only get to choose where it goes.{% endif %}">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://agicook.com/img/og/{% if r %}{{ rev }}{% else %}quiz{% endif %}.png">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{% if r %}{{ r.name }}: {{ r.tagline | replace("“", "") | replace("”", "") }}{% else %}Which Quantum Interpretation Are You? An instrument of self-measurement.{% endif %}">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,600;12..96,800&family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/quiz.css">
</head>
<body data-quiz-base="/which-quantum-interpretation-are-you/{{ route.base }}">

<nav class="site-nav">
  <a class="home" href="/">agicook</a>
  <span class="links">
    <a href="#glossary">glossary</a>
    <a href="/which-quantum-interpretation-are-you/v1/">v1</a>
  </span>
</nav>

<svg class="superpose" id="superpose" viewBox="0 0 600 700" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"></svg>

<main class="wrap">

  <!-- ---------- intro ---------- -->
  <section id="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">An instrument of self-measurement &middot; version 2</p>
    <h1>Which Quantum Interpretation<br>Are You<span class="qm">?</span></h1>
    <p class="dek">Ninety-nine years since anyone agreed on what a measurement is.
      Ten questions to find out which lump under the carpet is yours.</p>
    <p class="superpose-caption mono">You are currently in a superposition of
      seven results &mdash; all of them, with amplitudes, none of them yet yours</p>

    <div class="note">
      <p>Every [[no-go-theorem]] of the last sixty years has closed another exit
      marked &ldquo;common sense.&rdquo; [[bell]] ruled out one escape,
      [[contextuality]] another, [[pbr]] a third. What survives is a short list of
      theories that all agree with every experiment ever done and disagree
      violently about what is happening.</p>
      <p>None of them is sane. <strong>Weirdness is conserved</strong> &mdash; you
      only get to choose where it goes. This measures where you put it.</p>
      <p class="note-aside">Terms like <em>these</em> are explained on tap, and
      collected in the <a href="#glossary">glossary</a> at the foot of the page.</p>
    </div>

    <button class="btn-primary" id="begin">Begin measurement</button>

    <div class="debug" id="debug" hidden>
      <p class="debug-head mono">Debug &middot; play a full run</p>
      <div class="debug-links" id="debug-links"></div>
      <p class="debug-note mono">Local only. Unlike the roster links on a reveal, these
        synthesise a consistent playthrough &mdash; so &ldquo;How we caught you&rdquo; and
        the near-miss render too.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- quiz ---------- -->
  <section id="quiz" hidden>
    <div class="quiz-head">
      <p class="mono" id="counter">Question 1 of 9</p>
      <p class="mono" id="collapse-pct">Collapse: 0%</p>
    </div>
    <div class="collapse-bar"><div class="collapse-fill" id="collapse-fill"></div></div>

    <svg class="wavefn" id="wavefn" viewBox="0 0 600 120" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <path class="wave-fill" id="wave-fill" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></path>
      <path class="wave-line" id="wave-line" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></path>
    </svg>
    <p class="amps-caption mono">Your state, so far &mdash; which peak is which
      is not something you get to know before measuring</p>

    <h2 class="question" id="question"></h2>
    <div class="options" id="options"></div>

    <div class="quiz-foot">
      <button class="btn-ghost" id="back">Back</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- result ---------- -->
  <section id="result" hidden></section>

  <!-- ---------- glossary (also the no-JS fallback for every tooltip) ---------- -->
  <section id="glossary">
    <details class="glossary-block" id="glossary-block">
    <summary>Glossary <span class="count">{{ quiz.glossary | length }} terms</span></summary>
    <dl class="glossary">
      {%- for key, term in quiz.glossary %}
      <div class="gloss-entry" id="gloss-{{ key }}">
        <dt>{{ term.label }}</dt>
        <dd>
          <p class="gloss-short">{{ term.short }}</p>
          {%- if term.long %}<p class="gloss-long">{{ term.long }}</p>{% endif %}
          {%- if term.see %}
          <p class="gloss-see mono">See also:
            {%- for s in term.see %} <a href="#gloss-{{ s }}">{{ quiz.glossary[s].label }}</a>{{ "," if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}
          </p>
          {%- endif %}
        </dd>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
    </details>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="foot wrap">
  <a href="/">agicook</a>
  <a href="mailto:futurejira+human@gmail.com">email</a>
  <a href="/which-quantum-interpretation-are-you/v1/">version 1</a>
</footer>

{% from "motifs.njk" import base, fringes %}
{% include "motifs.njk" %}

<script type="application/json" id="q-questions">{{ quiz.questions | jsonscript | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="q-results">{{ quiz.results | jsonscript | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="q-meta">{{ quiz.meta | jsonscript | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="q-links">{{ quiz.links | jsonscript | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="q-glossary">{{ quiz.glossary | jsonscript | safe }}</script>
<script src="/js/gloss.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/share.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/quiz.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
